WEBVTT

00:03.811 --> 00:08.901
[indistinct chatter]

00:15.081 --> 00:16.911
Representing the graduates,

00:17.001 --> 00:19.331
Princess Liniana Dedoldia,

00:19.411 --> 00:22.501
and Princess Pursena Adoldia.

00:23.711 --> 00:26.501
Please step forward
to receive your diplomas

00:26.591 --> 00:28.881
and your credentials
as D-rank members

00:28.971 --> 00:30.551
of the Magic Guild.

00:30.631 --> 00:32.641
[♪ opening theme song playing]

01:57.051 --> 01:58.971
[♪ bright music playing]

01:59.721 --> 02:00.971
I was surprised to see you both

02:01.061 --> 02:02.731
at Linia
and Pursena's graduation.

02:02.811 --> 02:04.391
That was thoughtful of you.

02:04.481 --> 02:06.311
[ZANOBA]
Despite our differences,

02:06.401 --> 02:08.691
they have been
loyal to you, Master.

02:08.771 --> 02:10.401
And that being the case,

02:10.481 --> 02:11.901
clinging to a grudge
against them

02:11.991 --> 02:13.361
would ill become me.

02:14.151 --> 02:15.611
Yes, they're generally so crude,

02:15.701 --> 02:18.581
I hardly had anything to do
with them outside of class,

02:18.661 --> 02:20.281
but, as fellow students,

02:20.371 --> 02:22.661
I do consider them
my comrades in learning.

02:23.501 --> 02:25.671
So, I wanted to give them
a proper send-off.

02:27.461 --> 02:29.381
[RUDEUS] When I got here,
no one in the special class

02:29.461 --> 02:30.801
really got along,

02:30.881 --> 02:33.011
or even spoke
to each other very much.

02:34.221 --> 02:36.641
Seems like
everybody's growing up.

02:39.221 --> 02:41.771
-[knock on door]
-[RUDEUS] Nanahoshi.

02:41.851 --> 02:43.311
-May I?
-[NANAHOSHI] Go ahead.

02:44.231 --> 02:45.771
[Nanahoshi coughing]

02:46.481 --> 02:48.901
-Did you catch another cold?
-[coughs]

02:49.691 --> 02:51.111
Yeah, it would seem that way.

02:51.191 --> 02:53.071
[RUDEUS] Nanahoshi's health
hasn't been great

02:53.151 --> 02:54.401
for the past year.

02:54.491 --> 02:57.411
Dry coughing,
sudden fevers, the works.

02:58.861 --> 03:01.241
I always try to clear up
her symptoms when I can,

03:02.121 --> 03:04.911
but it never takes too long
before she's sick again.

03:05.001 --> 03:06.291
Detoxification magic

03:06.371 --> 03:08.791
can't fix an unhealthy body,
unfortunately.

03:08.871 --> 03:10.331
Perhaps you should consider

03:10.421 --> 03:12.631
taking your health
a little more seriously.

03:12.711 --> 03:14.881
I'm not just going to
lie around in bed.

03:14.961 --> 03:16.721
Not while my research
is going so well.

03:16.801 --> 03:18.181
[RUDEUS] She's not wrong.

03:18.261 --> 03:20.181
She's been
making great progress.

03:20.261 --> 03:22.431
She's up to phase three
of her plan now.

03:22.511 --> 03:24.521
The goal is
to summon something alive,

03:24.601 --> 03:26.601
such as a plant
or a small animal.

03:27.691 --> 03:29.861
Before long, we may be
able to grow vegetables

03:29.941 --> 03:31.191
from our old world here.

03:32.061 --> 03:33.191
Closer every day.

03:33.941 --> 03:35.741
So, are you ready
to get started?

03:35.821 --> 03:36.821
[knock on door]

03:36.901 --> 03:38.701
Hmm? It's open.

03:38.781 --> 03:39.951
[door opens]

03:40.031 --> 03:41.661
-[footsteps approaching]
-[ALL] Huh?

03:41.741 --> 03:43.241
Ex-mew-se us.

03:43.331 --> 03:44.831
Sorry to intrude.

03:44.911 --> 03:46.661
Heya, boss. You got a second?

03:46.751 --> 03:49.001
We've looked
all over the place for you.

03:49.081 --> 03:51.711
[RUDEUS]
I'm sensing a little hostility.

03:51.791 --> 03:53.421
Is it time for another duel?

03:54.131 --> 03:55.591
Maybe they wanna
settle the score

03:55.671 --> 03:57.171
before they leave forever?

03:57.761 --> 03:58.931
Come on!

03:59.011 --> 04:01.391
-Just follow us.
-We need you to.

04:01.471 --> 04:02.891
[RUDEUS] Mm.

04:03.391 --> 04:04.851
Well, why not?

04:04.931 --> 04:06.931
Feels wrong to turn them down.

04:07.021 --> 04:08.181
Yeah, you got it.

04:08.271 --> 04:10.561
Nanahoshi, I'll be right back.

04:10.651 --> 04:12.111
But what about our experiment?

04:12.191 --> 04:13.611
I did ask you first.

04:13.691 --> 04:15.021
[LINIA] Mew lot come too.

04:15.111 --> 04:17.491
Yeah, this here's
a special occasion.

04:17.571 --> 04:20.031
A once-in-a-lifetime opportunity
for the likes of mew.

04:20.111 --> 04:22.411
Excuse you!
What's this all about?

04:22.491 --> 04:23.871
And stop pulling!

04:23.951 --> 04:25.201
[ALL] Hmm?

04:25.281 --> 04:27.161
[♪ lively music playing]

04:31.291 --> 04:32.881
This will do fine.

04:32.961 --> 04:34.671
Brings back meowmories.

04:35.291 --> 04:36.761
[RUDEUS] Ah, yes.

04:36.841 --> 04:38.631
This is where
Zanoba and I kidnapped

04:38.711 --> 04:40.131
the two of them
a few years back.

04:40.931 --> 04:42.841
The first place we ever fought.

04:42.931 --> 04:45.681
Feels like an appropriate choice
of venue to me.

04:46.391 --> 04:48.391
[whispering] Sir, do you suppose

04:48.471 --> 04:50.731
this is leading up
to a rematch situation?

04:50.811 --> 04:51.851
[RUDEUS] Hmm.

04:54.151 --> 04:56.271
-It sure seems like it.
-Hmm.

04:57.361 --> 04:58.401
Uh.

05:01.701 --> 05:02.951
[BOTH] Oh.

05:03.241 --> 05:05.701
We want the boss and all of mew
to witness this, m'kay?

05:05.781 --> 05:07.371
What are you going to do?

05:07.451 --> 05:09.041
Linia and I are gonna find out

05:09.121 --> 05:11.661
which one of us is stronger
once and for all.

05:12.121 --> 05:13.581
My word, whatever for?

05:13.671 --> 05:17.381
Because the winner will become
chief of the Doldia Tribe.

05:17.461 --> 05:22.421
But the Dedoldia and Adoldia are
two separate clans, aren't they?

05:22.511 --> 05:25.051
Couldn't you each become
the chief of one of them?

05:25.141 --> 05:28.311
Myeah, we were talking
about that for a little while,

05:28.391 --> 05:29.851
until we clobbered
all the suitors

05:29.931 --> 05:32.351
who came last mating season,
then we said, "Forget it."

05:32.441 --> 05:33.771
Exactly.

05:34.151 --> 05:37.071
If we go back and fight at home,
the loser will get married off.

05:37.151 --> 05:40.111
And that'll be
a boring-ass snoozefest.

05:40.191 --> 05:42.451
It's an awful
big world out there.

05:43.071 --> 05:44.861
So why not live free instead?

05:44.951 --> 05:46.951
[LINIA]
No hard felines either way.

05:47.031 --> 05:48.831
[RUDEUS]
Welp, don't understand that.

05:48.911 --> 05:50.331
Yeah, I get that.

05:50.411 --> 05:53.411
You do what you need to.
We'll be here to bear witness.

05:53.501 --> 05:56.381
You really wanna help set up
a fight in the middle of campus?

05:56.461 --> 05:59.211
They'll do it either way.
We should be here for insurance.

05:59.301 --> 06:00.761
We owe mew one, boss!

06:00.841 --> 06:02.341
Yeah, thanks a bunch.

06:04.381 --> 06:06.721
[RUDEUS] From what I can tell,
they're pretty evenly matched.

06:07.641 --> 06:09.141
So without a judge,

06:09.221 --> 06:11.351
this may not
produce a clear victor.

06:12.811 --> 06:14.061
And not to be pedantic,

06:14.141 --> 06:16.651
but this isn't a "fight"
so much as a duel.

06:16.731 --> 06:19.271
They're competing for supremacy.

06:19.361 --> 06:20.361
[hisses]

06:20.441 --> 06:21.781
[growls]

06:23.281 --> 06:26.571
[RUDEUS] A deadly serious battle
between two beastfolk.

06:26.661 --> 06:28.031
Here we go.

06:28.121 --> 06:29.411
Listen up, Pursena,

06:29.491 --> 06:31.541
'cause I've been meaning
to say this for a while!

06:31.621 --> 06:34.121
I'm sick of your crap,
and I can't freakin' stand mew!

06:34.211 --> 06:35.791
You took the words
right outta my mouth!

06:35.871 --> 06:38.671
See, maybe if you
quit acting like an idiot

06:38.751 --> 06:41.001
and showed me some respect,
it'd be different!

06:41.091 --> 06:42.511
But you treat me
like I'm a child!

06:42.591 --> 06:43.711
Mew are!

06:43.801 --> 06:45.721
I was practically
your babysitter!

06:45.801 --> 06:47.511
Or do you need
a refresher on all the times

06:47.591 --> 06:49.091
I had to cover
for you wetting the bed

06:49.181 --> 06:50.681
when you should've outgrown it?!

06:50.761 --> 06:53.141
"Ooh, an Adoldia
never forgets a debt."

06:53.221 --> 06:54.311
What a joke!

06:54.641 --> 06:56.101
-You got the memory of a toad!
-[PURSENA] Nuh-uh!

06:56.191 --> 06:58.231
When you fell into the river
and almost drowned,

06:58.311 --> 06:59.981
who pulled you out?
That made us even!

07:00.071 --> 07:01.901
You're never gonna
find yourself a husband

07:01.981 --> 07:03.651
with that
ungrateful-ass attitude!

07:03.731 --> 07:05.151
Only 'cause
you just had to wipe out

07:05.241 --> 07:06.901
every last one of our suitors!

07:06.991 --> 07:08.451
You are so pathetic!

07:08.531 --> 07:09.661
Well, you smell weird!

07:09.741 --> 07:11.161
Well, you...

07:11.241 --> 07:13.161
You're fat!

07:13.241 --> 07:14.451
[gasps]

07:14.541 --> 07:17.211
You take that back!

07:17.291 --> 07:18.631
[yells]

07:18.711 --> 07:19.751
[both grunt]

07:22.381 --> 07:24.461
-[bells rings]
-[both grunting]

07:25.341 --> 07:27.131
And away we go!

07:27.221 --> 07:30.141
Pursena charges forward,
and Linia sends her packing!

07:30.221 --> 07:31.851
Pursena may have
the edge in power,

07:31.931 --> 07:33.771
but her opponent
is just a little faster!

07:33.851 --> 07:34.971
Pursena lets loose
with a right cross,

07:35.061 --> 07:36.561
and Linia is reeling!

07:36.641 --> 07:37.771
If this comes down
to a slugging match,

07:37.851 --> 07:38.771
Linia's in trouble!

07:38.851 --> 07:40.101
Pursena's not letting up!

07:40.191 --> 07:41.941
Will Linia run,
or will she hold her ground?

07:42.021 --> 07:43.611
Ooh, she held her ground!

07:43.691 --> 07:45.731
She dishes out a left,
and then a right!

07:45.821 --> 07:47.111
Pursena's taking some hits here,

07:47.201 --> 07:48.741
but this girl's
a bloodhound, gang,

07:48.821 --> 07:50.491
and she's still
got her prey on the ropes!

07:50.571 --> 07:51.741
Ooh-hoo!

07:52.031 --> 07:54.331
Looks like we got a wardrobe
malfunction, everybody!

07:54.411 --> 07:56.411
We may have to cut
to commercial, here!

07:56.501 --> 07:58.211
Let's go to Zanoba
for the color.

07:58.291 --> 07:59.211
[Linia, Pursena grunting]

07:59.291 --> 08:01.501
Uh. [clears throat]

08:01.581 --> 08:03.671
Pursena closes the distance
for the in-fight!

08:03.751 --> 08:05.671
Linia's reflexes
keep her just out of reach,

08:05.761 --> 08:07.551
but the butterfly
has lost her wings!

08:07.631 --> 08:09.971
She ain't got the speed anymore
for the hit-run game!

08:10.051 --> 08:12.681
Is this the end?
No! Linia digs in her fangs

08:12.761 --> 08:14.641
and then tackles Pursena
to the ground!

08:14.721 --> 08:16.811
But wait!
Pursena has fangs of her own!

08:16.891 --> 08:18.021
Look at those chompers!

08:18.101 --> 08:20.271
This could be
the match of the century!

08:20.351 --> 08:22.101
What an unseemly way to fight.

08:22.191 --> 08:24.901
They're more like roughhousing
children than warriors.

08:25.401 --> 08:27.741
Well, yeah, I guess
that's a fair observation.

08:28.361 --> 08:30.531
Listen.
I hate to be a killjoy here,

08:30.611 --> 08:32.491
but it seems like
a big deal to them,

08:32.571 --> 08:34.121
so maybe give it a rest.

08:35.701 --> 08:36.621
[chuckles awkwardly]

08:36.701 --> 08:38.161
No, you're right.

08:41.961 --> 08:45.291
[both grunting]

08:51.261 --> 08:53.091
[Pursena panting]

08:56.141 --> 08:57.471
That settles that.

08:58.351 --> 09:00.061
[bell ringing]

09:01.231 --> 09:02.061
[RUDEUS] Brilliant.

09:02.151 --> 09:03.271
Breathtaking!

09:03.351 --> 09:04.691
Beautiful.

09:04.771 --> 09:06.571
She had fought for her life,

09:06.651 --> 09:08.191
and emerged triumphant.

09:09.531 --> 09:10.531
[sighs]

09:11.031 --> 09:11.951
Mm.

09:15.951 --> 09:17.621
See that? I did it.

09:18.411 --> 09:19.951
[RUDEUS] Yeah, congratulations.

09:20.041 --> 09:21.541
Let me fix that before you scar.

09:22.501 --> 09:25.461
No, thanks.
I really don't mind if it does.

09:25.541 --> 09:27.591
My wounds are a badge of honor.

09:28.051 --> 09:30.381
Plus, she and I may
never see each other again,

09:30.471 --> 09:31.971
so I want something
to remember her by.

09:32.051 --> 09:33.181
[both gasp]

09:33.261 --> 09:34.891
But surely you're
gonna stick together

09:34.971 --> 09:36.761
until you leave town, at least?

09:37.811 --> 09:39.021
[PURSENA] Gonna go
our separate ways

09:39.101 --> 09:40.391
right here and now.

09:40.481 --> 09:42.771
Already got our bags
packed and everything.

09:44.151 --> 09:46.401
[RUDEUS] They must have
agreed to that ahead of time.

09:47.061 --> 09:49.981
To say goodbye
where their paths diverge.

09:52.651 --> 09:54.491
That's kinda poetic.

09:55.701 --> 09:57.491
Well, you should
still get patched up

09:57.571 --> 09:59.161
even if it's not with magic.

09:59.241 --> 10:00.621
I know. I will.

10:00.701 --> 10:03.121
Boss, you've been a real one.

10:13.131 --> 10:14.591
[RUDEUS]
My friends are all right.

10:17.431 --> 10:18.511
Now...

10:22.311 --> 10:24.431
Aw, man, she's dead.

10:25.481 --> 10:26.861
Tell my story.

10:27.361 --> 10:28.481
You don't look so hot.

10:29.401 --> 10:30.691
Don't feel so hot.

10:33.191 --> 10:34.861
Appreciate ya, boss.

10:36.531 --> 10:37.701
[sighs]

10:37.781 --> 10:39.661
Can't believe I lost.

10:39.741 --> 10:41.031
Hell of a fight, though.

10:41.121 --> 10:44.081
I could hear mew
on the sidelines the whole time.

10:44.161 --> 10:46.331
Sounded like mew
were enjoying yourself.

10:46.961 --> 10:49.131
[RUDEUS] Yeah,
I didn't do a great job

10:49.211 --> 10:51.421
reading the room on this one.
That's on me.

10:51.501 --> 10:53.301
But it really was
an exciting match.

10:53.381 --> 10:55.551
Probably just looked like
one of our regular fights

10:55.631 --> 10:57.141
from where you were standin',

10:57.221 --> 10:59.761
but it's nice that
someone was here to enjoy it.

10:59.851 --> 11:02.181
Gotta take your fun
where you can.

11:02.271 --> 11:04.181
No healing magic
for you, either?

11:04.271 --> 11:07.651
Mewsually, I like to try
and erase any signs that I lost,

11:07.731 --> 11:10.561
but for these, I think
it's okay to make an exception.

11:10.651 --> 11:12.731
Wait long enough,
and maybe it'll be somethin'

11:12.821 --> 11:14.691
to brag about,
you know what I mean?

11:15.241 --> 11:17.071
They are honorable wounds.

11:17.151 --> 11:19.661
Granted, I don't know much
of beastfolk duels,

11:19.741 --> 11:22.201
nonetheless, I found
the display most riveting.

11:22.281 --> 11:25.041
I didn't figure on getting
compliments from mew.

11:25.121 --> 11:27.751
Pretty big change from when you
kidnapped us out here, eh?

11:28.831 --> 11:31.291
Really, I'm sorry
about your doll, by the way.

11:31.381 --> 11:33.551
Please. My master has
long since pardoned you

11:33.631 --> 11:34.801
for that incident.

11:34.881 --> 11:35.841
As have I.

11:36.301 --> 11:38.721
May we part knowing
that I bear you no ill will.

11:39.341 --> 11:40.391
Hmm.

11:44.771 --> 11:46.681
[RUDEUS] So,
what do you plan to do now?

11:47.771 --> 11:49.651
[LINIA] Travel
wherever the road takes me,

11:49.731 --> 11:51.651
and start up my own store.

11:51.731 --> 11:53.231
[RUDEUS] Her own store?

11:53.321 --> 11:54.781
I can't imagine that'll go well.

11:54.861 --> 11:57.611
I hope you have
an actual plan worked out.

11:57.691 --> 11:59.451
Mew bet I do.

11:59.531 --> 12:02.321
[RUDEUS] If she has a vision,
maybe she'll be okay.

12:03.121 --> 12:04.791
Nope, I still can't imagine it.

12:04.871 --> 12:07.251
I have a funny feeling
she's gonna open up a shop

12:07.331 --> 12:10.581
with some half-assed ideas
and land herself in hot water.

12:11.251 --> 12:12.591
Five years from meow,

12:12.671 --> 12:14.881
I'll be rolling around
in big 'ol piles of cash.

12:15.711 --> 12:18.051
[RUDEUS] Well, you know
if you ever run into trouble,

12:18.131 --> 12:20.011
you can always come
to me for help.

12:20.091 --> 12:21.931
[ZANOBA]
And I will assist you as well.

12:22.011 --> 12:23.761
[Linia laughs]
Once I hit it big,

12:23.851 --> 12:25.931
you'll be the ones
borrowing money from me!

12:30.101 --> 12:32.981
[RUDEUS] Are they really never
going to see each other again?

12:33.811 --> 12:35.861
I mean, they were inseparable.

12:37.441 --> 12:39.111
I know it's gotta be tough,

12:39.781 --> 12:40.781
but I can't help but think

12:40.861 --> 12:42.781
it's kind
of a cool way to be too.

12:45.831 --> 12:47.041
Wouldn't you know it,

12:47.121 --> 12:48.751
later that evening,

12:48.831 --> 12:51.291
a little birdie told me
about two beast women

12:51.371 --> 12:55.341
covered in bandages, squabbling
in the back of a stagecoach.

12:55.421 --> 12:57.801
I bet neither of them checked
when the carriages left,

12:57.881 --> 12:59.761
and ended up
booking the same one.

12:59.841 --> 13:01.591
Okay, now that's poetic.

13:01.681 --> 13:02.971
[arguing]

13:10.481 --> 13:11.981
Ready. Please begin.

13:13.861 --> 13:15.861
Okay, I'll start
channeling the mana now.

13:18.901 --> 13:21.571
Oh, man,
it takes a hell of a lot.

13:21.651 --> 13:24.031
Could anyone but me
even use the damn thing?

13:25.371 --> 13:26.781
Seems this will take a while.

13:26.871 --> 13:28.581
-Maybe we should work to--
-Hush.

13:30.331 --> 13:31.411
[all gasp]

13:35.171 --> 13:37.091
[RUDEUS]
That glow was too familiar.

13:37.711 --> 13:38.921
This is exactly what I saw

13:39.011 --> 13:40.921
right before
the mass teleportation.

13:42.971 --> 13:45.051
Oh, crap, should I stop?

13:45.141 --> 13:46.971
This world
couldn't handle that again.

13:48.101 --> 13:50.811
No. We've done
our homework specifically

13:50.891 --> 13:52.981
so nothing like that can happen.

13:53.601 --> 13:55.061
We have nothing to worry about.

13:55.151 --> 13:56.231
We can do this!

14:07.031 --> 14:08.621
[all gasp]

14:09.661 --> 14:11.121
[gasps excitedly]

14:12.001 --> 14:13.161
How about that?

14:13.751 --> 14:16.581
[gasps] It worked!

14:16.671 --> 14:18.921
[ZANOBA]
Congratulations to you, Master!

14:19.001 --> 14:19.921
[CLIFF] Success!

14:20.551 --> 14:23.051
Still, those stripes look
awfully sinister, don't they?

14:23.131 --> 14:24.471
You sure it's safe to hold?

14:24.551 --> 14:25.591
Oh, yes.

14:25.681 --> 14:27.431
Do be careful
not to drop it, though.

14:27.511 --> 14:28.931
It's big, but fragile.

14:29.011 --> 14:30.681
Hey, Nanahoshi.

14:30.771 --> 14:33.351
Watermelons don't exist
in this world yet, right?

14:33.431 --> 14:35.391
Does that mean it came
from the other world?

14:35.481 --> 14:36.941
Yeah, most likely,

14:37.021 --> 14:38.441
though it's not like
I have much control

14:38.521 --> 14:40.151
over what I summon anyway.

14:41.071 --> 14:43.781
Honestly, I was just trying
to summon a cabbage.

14:44.491 --> 14:47.071
[RUDEUS] This world does have
vegetables similar to cabbages.

14:47.991 --> 14:49.321
Could we really
tell the difference

14:49.411 --> 14:50.831
from an other-world vegetable?

14:50.911 --> 14:52.201
[indistinct chatter]

14:52.291 --> 14:53.451
[RUDEUS]
Maybe our plan to summon a plant

14:53.541 --> 14:55.331
was flawed from the start.

14:55.411 --> 14:57.581
Should we have picked
a different specimen?

14:57.671 --> 15:00.421
You can try a bite later
and taste it for yourself.

15:01.291 --> 15:02.961
[RUDEUS] No, it's fine.

15:03.051 --> 15:04.761
Sure, we may have
summoned a watermelon

15:04.841 --> 15:06.261
instead of a cabbage,

15:06.341 --> 15:08.181
but I'd still
call that a success.

15:08.261 --> 15:10.601
Well, if we have succeeded,
as you said,

15:10.681 --> 15:12.011
we should celebrate tonight.

15:12.101 --> 15:13.681
[RUDEUS] Yeah, you're right.

15:14.181 --> 15:15.891
[ALL] Cheers!

15:16.811 --> 15:18.691
[RUDEUS] I don't know
when it started exactly,

15:18.771 --> 15:22.231
but we party whenever one of us
has something to celebrate.

15:22.321 --> 15:25.491
We'd lost Linia and Pursena
since the last one,

15:25.571 --> 15:27.611
but this time,
Roxy and Norn joined in.

15:29.241 --> 15:30.621
Badigadi isn't here, either,

15:30.701 --> 15:33.031
so we're missing
the liveliest members,

15:33.621 --> 15:36.251
but I don't think
the overall mood has changed.

15:36.331 --> 15:40.131
Anyway, for once,
Nanahoshi was happy.

15:40.211 --> 15:42.001
Here, Rudy, have some more.

15:42.671 --> 15:45.381
Thank you.
Are you not drinking tonight?

15:45.461 --> 15:48.891
Not tonight.
I get so silly when I'm tipsy.

15:48.971 --> 15:50.601
I was thinking I'd abstain.

15:50.681 --> 15:52.101
Suit yourself.

15:52.181 --> 15:54.681
Remember, we're not spending
the night here this time.

15:54.771 --> 15:57.351
We're going home
so we can tuck Lucie into bed.

15:57.431 --> 15:58.641
Oh, yeah, I know that.

15:58.731 --> 16:00.611
Shame she won't drink.

16:00.691 --> 16:01.981
She's an adorable drunk.

16:02.061 --> 16:03.821
-Rudy.
-Huh?

16:03.901 --> 16:06.111
Would you please pull out
your chair a little bit?

16:08.151 --> 16:09.401
[sighs]

16:09.491 --> 16:12.121
-Roxy, are you drunk right now?
-A little.

16:12.201 --> 16:14.451
I'd like to
try that later, okay?

16:14.911 --> 16:16.121
Yeah, of course!

16:16.751 --> 16:18.291
Hell, I'd be more than happy

16:18.371 --> 16:21.671
to have Roxy on my left knee
and Sylphie on my right.

16:21.751 --> 16:22.841
[NORN] Brother.

16:24.461 --> 16:26.461
Am I embarrassing you, Norn?

16:26.551 --> 16:27.551
Sorry 'bout that.

16:27.631 --> 16:29.301
Oh, no, it's nothing like that.

16:29.381 --> 16:32.971
I, uh, was just wanting
to talk to you about something.

16:33.051 --> 16:34.101
You got a sec?

16:34.551 --> 16:35.891
I do. What's up?

16:35.971 --> 16:37.521
[NORN] Okay.

16:37.601 --> 16:40.351
Well, it--
it's about the student council.

16:40.441 --> 16:42.361
Oh, I see.

16:42.441 --> 16:44.021
I hadn't thought
about it until now,

16:44.651 --> 16:47.151
but Norn was with them
at the graduation.

16:47.241 --> 16:49.741
Miss Ariel,
she invited me to join.

16:49.821 --> 16:50.741
[gasps]

16:51.281 --> 16:53.951
She's aware that my grades
aren't particularly good,

16:54.031 --> 16:56.491
but she said
people gravitate towards me.

16:56.581 --> 16:58.581
Like I have a special gift.

16:58.661 --> 17:00.211
You don't say.

17:00.291 --> 17:03.831
You know, I have heard Norn
was pretty popular at school.

17:03.921 --> 17:05.631
Did you know
about this, Sylphie?

17:06.091 --> 17:07.551
Yup. I'd heard.

17:07.631 --> 17:09.551
[RUDEUS] So she knew about it.

17:09.631 --> 17:11.341
-Maybe Roxy did too.
-Uh.

17:13.511 --> 17:15.301
[RUDEUS]
Was I the only one in the dark?

17:15.391 --> 17:17.851
-I can't believe it.
-Sorry about that.

17:17.931 --> 17:18.971
I thought
that it would be better

17:19.061 --> 17:20.641
for Norn to tell you herself.

17:20.731 --> 17:21.771
It's okay.

17:22.441 --> 17:24.111
So, now that you know,

17:24.191 --> 17:27.231
would you mind if I officially
join the student council?

17:27.321 --> 17:28.821
Of course--

17:28.901 --> 17:31.611
Wait, isn't Norn
focusing on swordplay

17:31.701 --> 17:33.241
and writing at the moment?

17:33.321 --> 17:34.451
Can she handle the pressures

17:34.531 --> 17:37.031
of student council work
on top of that?

17:37.951 --> 17:39.791
-It's just that...
-[NORN] Yes?

17:39.871 --> 17:43.081
...I'm not opposed to you
accepting Ariel's invitation,

17:43.161 --> 17:45.171
as long as it's not
too much to take on.

17:45.791 --> 17:47.171
I'm concerned
that your schoolwork

17:47.251 --> 17:49.301
will be more difficult
in your third year.

17:50.051 --> 17:51.551
I'll keep working hard
on my writing

17:51.631 --> 17:53.721
and sword training,
and school too.

17:54.641 --> 17:57.511
[RUDEUS] That's easier said
than done, but still.

17:57.851 --> 17:58.811
[sighs]

17:59.311 --> 18:00.811
-[SYLPHIETTE] Rudy.
-Hmm?

18:01.391 --> 18:02.391
It's fine.

18:02.481 --> 18:04.231
She's stayed
on top of her duties,

18:04.771 --> 18:06.981
and she's already been
helping the student council

18:07.061 --> 18:08.651
for well over a year now.

18:08.731 --> 18:11.071
What? You mean,
she's been doing it

18:11.151 --> 18:13.781
since before I started
her sword training?

18:13.861 --> 18:16.321
[chuckles]
She can handle this too.

18:16.411 --> 18:17.741
I guarantee it.

18:18.951 --> 18:20.161
[RUDEUS] I get it.

18:20.241 --> 18:21.661
She already proved
she can do it,

18:21.751 --> 18:23.041
it's not about that.

18:23.661 --> 18:26.251
In which case,
who am I to tell her no?

18:26.961 --> 18:28.791
You have been working hard.

18:29.591 --> 18:31.591
Well, I don't think
you need my permission,

18:31.671 --> 18:33.091
but you've got it anyway.

18:34.841 --> 18:36.261
I can't thank you enough!

18:38.181 --> 18:39.721
[NANAHOSHI] Hey, everyone!

18:39.811 --> 18:41.811
I hope you're ready
to try some watermelon!

18:41.891 --> 18:45.191
[RUDEUS] In the end,
how it turns out is up to her.

18:45.851 --> 18:47.101
Nanahoshi gets results

18:47.191 --> 18:49.151
because she's
putting in the effort.

18:49.231 --> 18:51.401
The same goes
for Linia and Pursena.

18:52.481 --> 18:54.611
Still, I think
it's our duty as adults

18:54.691 --> 18:56.661
to support the kids
and cheer them on.

18:57.661 --> 18:58.951
I wouldn't be who I am now

18:59.031 --> 19:01.541
if the people in my life
hadn't done the same.

19:02.121 --> 19:06.041
So, I'll always be ready
to support them too.

19:09.251 --> 19:10.381
[Nanahoshi coughs]

19:10.961 --> 19:12.961
Thank you for-- [coughing]

19:13.051 --> 19:14.301
Are you okay?

19:14.381 --> 19:17.641
-[coughing]
-I can cast detoxification.

19:17.721 --> 19:19.681
I got Sylphie
to cast it on me earlier,

19:19.761 --> 19:20.971
so I'm good for now.

19:21.061 --> 19:23.641
Anyway,
because you helped me again,

19:23.721 --> 19:26.231
I can move on
to the next phase now.

19:26.311 --> 19:28.731
The next phase is
to summon a living being

19:28.811 --> 19:31.151
that meets some kind
of specific criteria?

19:31.231 --> 19:33.401
That's right.
I know an expert in the field,

19:33.481 --> 19:35.611
so I'm going to ask
for his guidance.

19:35.691 --> 19:36.861
[RUDEUS] Ah, yes.

19:36.951 --> 19:39.071
The "authority
on summoning" himself.

19:41.031 --> 19:44.201
Hey, it's, uh,
not Orsted, is it?

19:44.291 --> 19:46.001
-No, it's not.
-[sighs]

19:47.001 --> 19:49.421
On that note, I have a proposal.

19:49.501 --> 19:52.551
You know how I still owe you
for the bottle-cap experiment?

19:52.631 --> 19:56.131
Oh, now that you mention it,
I do remember that, yeah.

19:56.211 --> 19:58.051
I can introduce you to him,

19:58.131 --> 20:00.721
as your reward
for helping me with both phases.

20:00.801 --> 20:02.051
If you want, that is.

20:02.141 --> 20:03.851
Meet the mage, huh?

20:03.931 --> 20:05.271
Is this guy such a big deal

20:05.351 --> 20:07.811
that simply meeting him
is worth two rewards?

20:07.891 --> 20:10.191
Oh, yes. I'd say so.

20:10.271 --> 20:11.811
There's even a chance
he could do something

20:11.901 --> 20:13.901
to help with your mother's
memory loss.

20:16.151 --> 20:17.071
Really?

20:18.401 --> 20:20.111
Be honest, is that true?

20:20.201 --> 20:21.991
[NANAHOSHI] I can't be certain,

20:22.071 --> 20:25.371
but he's lived a long time,
so if anyone can, it's him.

20:25.451 --> 20:26.451
[gasps]

20:27.501 --> 20:30.171
I think Zenith is
making a steady recovery,

20:30.251 --> 20:33.131
but it's hard to know if her
memories will ever fully return.

20:34.551 --> 20:36.751
Even if he can't cure her,

20:36.841 --> 20:39.471
there's a chance he'll have
a name for her condition,

20:39.551 --> 20:41.471
or has seen similar cases.

20:42.431 --> 20:45.141
I guess there's some reason you
couldn't introduce us sooner,

20:45.221 --> 20:47.061
since you're just telling me
about him now.

20:47.141 --> 20:50.311
There is. Sorry, but I have
my own stuff to deal with.

20:50.941 --> 20:53.861
Are you discussing
Lady Nanahoshi's master?

20:53.941 --> 20:56.361
If you're offering
introductions now,

20:56.441 --> 20:58.191
I'd like to meet him myself.

20:58.281 --> 21:00.451
I mean, you helped as well,

21:00.531 --> 21:02.951
so I guess I really
wouldn't mind introducing you.

21:03.031 --> 21:05.951
Um, I'm kind of interested too.

21:06.041 --> 21:09.581
Would it be a problem if we all
showed up as a big group?

21:09.661 --> 21:11.081
I don't think so.

21:11.161 --> 21:13.711
He said that he could
handle 12 guests at once.

21:14.341 --> 21:17.001
How long do you think it'll take
to get to him?

21:17.091 --> 21:19.171
No more than a day,
at the very most.

21:19.261 --> 21:21.381
Wow. He's local, then?

21:21.471 --> 21:23.801
You think we've already met,
by any chance?

21:24.431 --> 21:26.641
[NANAHOSHI] He's not local,
and you haven't met him.

21:26.721 --> 21:28.351
But I know a way for you to.

21:28.931 --> 21:30.101
Okay.

21:30.181 --> 21:32.851
Well then,
what's this guy's name?

21:34.521 --> 21:35.481
Mm.

21:38.321 --> 21:40.571
His name stays between us.

21:40.651 --> 21:41.571
Okay?

21:41.651 --> 21:42.571
[ALL] Mm.

21:45.531 --> 21:47.451
He is known as Perugius.

21:47.541 --> 21:48.741
[all gasp]

21:49.991 --> 21:52.621
[RUDEUS] Perugius,
the Armored Dragon King.

21:52.711 --> 21:55.751
One of the three heroes
who killed the Demon God.

21:55.831 --> 21:59.501
A man who led humanity
to victory in the Laplace War,

21:59.591 --> 22:01.971
four hundred years ago.

22:05.091 --> 22:07.051
[♪ closing theme song playing]
